[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_inydl"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_inydl")
source = "# Cache: gem trader. Sells skill and support gems, explains how they fit together.
~ start
Cache: Ah. A fresh process. Looking to compile something new?
* Show me your gems. -> shop
* What's the difference between skill and support gems? -> about_gems
* How do I use them? -> how_to
* Goodbye. -> bye

~ shop
> open_shop

~ about_gems
Cache: Skill gems are functions. Strike, Slam, Blast. Each one does a thing when you call it.
Cache: Support gems are modifiers. Alone they do nothing. Linked to a skill, they change how it runs.
Cache: Explode on kill, more damage, wider area... One skill, many builds.
* And scripting? -> about_scripts
* Got it. -> start

~ about_scripts
Cache: Socket a gem, then open the SCRIPTING tab. Every gem gives you knobs to turn.
Cache: Buffs cost points. Drawbacks give points back. Use few blocks and the code runs cleaner. Bonus damage, too.
Cache: Supports add their own knobs to the skill they're linked to. More gems, more options.
* Back. -> start

~ how_to
Cache: Press K. Drop a skill gem in a socket, then link supports beside it.
Cache: Bind the skill to a key, and it's yours.
Cache: Gems don't level from use here. Find better ones, or buy them from me.
* Back. -> start

~ bye
Cache: Come back when your code needs more functions.
-> end"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
